# Story 14: Panes Overview (45s)
# Hook: One window, many minds. Every pane is its own shell and its own AI agent.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-014-panes-overview.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
One window, many minds. Every pane is its own shell and its own AI agent.

[00:04.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and you get a single pane -- a full terminal backed by its own agent.

[00:09.0 --> 00:16.0]
Press Ctrl+N to create another pane. Instantly you have two independent terminals side by side.

[00:16.0 --> 00:23.0]
Add as many as you like. Each pane has its own working directory, its own history, its own AI context.

[00:23.0 --> 00:33.0]
Press Tab to cycle through your panes. The focused pane gets a highlighted border.

[00:33.0 --> 00:40.0]
Whatever you type lands only in the pane you've focused -- the others keep running on their own.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Ctrl+N to add a pane, Tab to move between them. That's the foundation of every Rysh layout.

